# Dispo command surface

## Needs attention

One panel resolves active problems. No modal chains, no “press F5”, no dead ends.

For each item (no bus, missing/sick driver, wrong code, report, coverage hole, supported incident types):

1. Show problem, affected trip/group, ops impact
2. Safe options in the **same** panel
3. One clear Apply
4. Stay pending until server responds
5. Success → confirm + refresh canonical state
6. Reject → rollback optimistic UI, keep context, readable error
7. Conflict → offer refreshed state + re-choose; **never** silent overwrite

Health/banners/alerts deep-link into the matching item + action.

## Pool order (drivers & buses)

1. This group — free  
2. Company — free or unassigned  
3. Other groups — free  

Unavailable candidates must not assign successfully even if stale client still lists them.

## Concurrency (existing mechanisms only)

- Shifts: `expectedRevision` / project revision guards (`D6`)
- Buses: `bus.revision` + `expectedRevision` (`D22`)
- No “why did you change this?” forms — toast + refresh from server on conflict
- Soft-remove / guided incidents stay aligned with Live Issues ↔ Needs attention

## Canonical plan

`shifts/{driverId}_{date}` is SoT; `schedules` is server-owned monthly projection. Do not invent a second temporary SoT for UI convenience.
